.TITLE "dir"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Lists directory contents. It displays information about files and directories within the current or specified path and is a fundamental tool for __filesystem navigation__ in Windows.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**dir**
Lists the names of files and directories in the current path.
> 

**dir /p**
Pauses after each screen of information.
> __/p__ pause flag

**dir /w**
Displays the list in wide format, showing only names.
> __/w__ wide format flag

**dir /a**
Displays files with specified attributes, including hidden files.
> __/a__ attributes flag

**dir /s**
Displays files in the specified directory and all subdirectories.
> __/s__ subdirectories flag

**dir /o:n**
Sorts the list alphabetically by name.
> __/o:n__ sort by name flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __dir /s__ is helpful for finding files across multiple folders. Combine __/a__ with __/p__ to view hidden system files one screen at a time.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:cd** **windows:mkdir** **windows:type**

